{"nodes": [{"id": "changelog_document", "label": "DevView CHANGELOG.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_openapi_migration", "label": "Migration from mocks.json to OpenAPI 3.x spec parsing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "31-38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "NetworkMock moved from a bespoke mocks.json config to parsing real OpenAPI 3.x documents so one spec file maps to one API group; the environment axis was removed entirely because a spec's servers[] list already supplies request-matching hosts, making a separate environment dimension redundant when an app talks to two hosts for the same API."}, {"id": "changelog_apigroupconfig_apispec_rename", "label": "ApiGroupConfig -> ApiSpec vocabulary rename (networkmock)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "39-45", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Renamed ApiGroupConfig/EndpointConfig/EndpointKey/EndpointDescriptor/EndpointMockState/GroupEnvironmentUiModel/EndpointUiModel to OpenAPI vocabulary (ApiSpec/Operation/OperationKey/OperationDescriptor/OperationMockState/ApiSpecUiModel/OperationUiModel) to match the new OpenAPI-based engine; MockResponse and MockMatch were deliberately left unrenamed since they model DevView's own runtime mocking behavior, not something OpenAPI itself describes."}, {"id": "changelog_timecapsuleeffect_subtitle_change", "label": "TimeCapsuleEffect subtitle parameter (breaking change)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "63-65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A new subtitle parameter was inserted between label and maxEntries on TimeCapsuleEffect so the 